cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the methodology or the toolbox, please cite the repository."
title: "paired-eval: a paired-evaluation toolbox for LLM models, agents and harnesses"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-09-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alloevil/paired-eval"
url: "https://github.com/alloevil/paired-eval"
keywords:
  - llm-evaluation
  - paired-comparison
  - mutation-testing
  - statistics
authors:
  - name: "paired-eval contributors"
abstract: >-
  Evaluate LLM models, agents and harnesses: programmatic checks first (exact / program /
  retrieval / trajectory grounding), rubrics only for what cannot be verified, with a gated
  program-then-rubric composition; every comparison is an interleaved paired A/B with honest
  statistics (McNemar, permutation, Holm, minimum detectable effect, p-value floor). Zero dependencies.
